\date{2026-04-07T14:32:06Z}
\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Example}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{What is the result of dividing #{-24} by #{11}? If we think purely in terms of “how many copies of #{11} will fit” we might think the quotient is #{-2}, but that would result in a remainder of #{-2}, which is not in the required range! In fact, #{-24 = 11 \cdot (-3) + 9}, so the quotient is #{-3} with a remainder of #{9}.}
